    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster presents a high-ceiling core today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our premier efficiency score of 81.88. His massive projection is driven by a potent combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a dynamic platoon advantage against Flaherty. Joining him as a primary engine is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.35), who exploits the matchup against Elder; the combination of a favorable SP_xERA and a premier #2 spot in the order elevates his production floor significantly above his season baseline. Meanwhile, **Josh Jung** (61.62) provides a surprisingly strong secondary play as he faces the league-high xERA of 5.91 from Grayson Rodriguez, allowing us to leverage his superior situational upside.\n\nEfficiency remains the priority as we balance game caps against scarcity. **Sam Antonacci** (48.07) stays in the lineup despite the tough matchup against Trevor McDonald because his #1 lineup spot and wind-aided park factors offer a unique opportunity to chase stolen bases, which remain our most critical scarcity lever. On the bench, **Dominic Smith** (43.10) was the closest exclusion; while his profile is solid, he was ultimately outpaced by the higher offensive potential of our starting cohort. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several players, particularly **Josh Lowe** and **Jackson Merrill**; **Josh Lowe** faces a difficult challenge against deGrom, whose presence significantly suppresses his score (48.35), but his potential to contribute to our stolen base tally forces his inclusion over high-upside bench depth. \n\nRisks are concentrated in the late-afternoon window, specifically for **Kyle Tucker** (53.10) and **Andy Pages** (44.56), both of whom must contend with Henderson\u2019s elite pitching profile. We have prioritized lineup positioning for these hitters to mitigate the SP skill drag, but these positions remain the most vulnerable to underperformance. We continue to monitor the status of **Miguel Vargas** and **Nolan Schanuel** should any late-scratch lineup changes occur, but for now, the optimizer favors the aggressive deployment of our speed-capable assets to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 landscape.",
